    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87606" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκαθηγ-έομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go before and guide,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.95.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς εὐνοίας -ηγουμένης πρός τινας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					5.86.10
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. κρίσεων</span>
			<i>influence</i> decisions <i>beforehand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.6.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς . . θεοῖς π. τῶν ἀγαθῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					4.133c
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be a forerunner, pioneer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Metrod.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be precedent,</i> opp. consequent or subsequent, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.101
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				116
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
